body:
When the field is quiet, Joren's Sending finds you, and it smells of rain.

'You fought in the storm's weather,' he says. 'I felt it. It was loud the whole time, and half of what it said was his.' A gust, and the borrowed voice: 'This was read a long time ago.' Then his own, tired: 'That half. Never mind that half. Under it, between the gusts, it was saying something of its own. It used to. What did it want?'

{shadow}

Joren's Sending reaches you with frost in it.

'You fought in the ice's weather,' he says. 'The cold, the white, the air that will not move. The ice was there. It has not come to the table since the hall. The storm talks over it, and the ice does not argue with people who talk over it. It waits. But it was in that fight with you. What did it want?'

{shadow}

The Sending comes hot, and smells of ash.

'You fought under the ash,' Joren says. 'The fire was there. It walked out of my table a month ago, and it has been burning across three regions to make a point. You heard it. What did it want?'

{shadow}
